      "edition": "Tuesday 3 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Staff decision",
          "heading": "Borthwick turned down Shaun Edwards's offer to work at England's World Cup",
          "body": "Shaun Edwards says he told Steve Borthwick he would take any role on England's staff, even \"assistant kit man\", but the head coach was content with his set-up. Borthwick's defence structure for Australia 2027 is already settled, with Richard Wigglesworth overseeing it alongside Byron McGuigan and Joe El-Abd. Edwards, 60, who left France earlier this year, has instead signed with Argentina until the end of the tournament."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
