      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Court appearance",
          "heading": "Former Ireland cap Brendan Mullin contests perfume theft charge in Dublin court",
          "body": "Mullin, accused of stealing Hermès perfume worth €158 from Brown Thomas on Dublin's Grafton Street in May, told Dublin District Court he was pleading not guilty. The 62-year-old, who won 55 Ireland caps between 1984 and 1995, represented himself because of a row with the Minister for Justice over legal aid reforms that has led many solicitors to withdraw from District Court cases. Judge John Hughes set eight March as the hearing date and remanded him on continuing bail."
