      "edition": "Tuesday 3 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Youth spotlight",
          "heading": "Steff Emanuel shines as Cardiff beat Ospreys 26-0 in Welsh derby",
          "body": "Emanuel was the standout in Cardiff's emphatic derby win at St Helen's, the 20-year-old centre credited with helping create three tries, including both of Tom Bowen's and Josh Adams' touchdowns. He also held up Keelan Giles over the line late on to protect the clean sheet, finishing with 15 carries and 17 tackles. Tom Shanklin called the performance \"probably perfect\", and Jonathan Davies suggested Emanuel could one day be an option for Wales at inside centre if they persist with a playmaker at 12."
        },
