      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "England rule out Alex Mitchell and Archie McParland for Wallabies Test",
          "body": "England's preparations for the Wallabies have been hit hard at scrumhalf, with Northampton's Alex Mitchell facing a scan on a hamstring injury and McParland sidelined by a calf problem sustained at training camp. Steve Borthwick has called up Ben Spencer and Harry Randall to cover, while first-choice fly-half Fin Smith is battling a calf strain and has until Wednesday to prove his fitness. Borthwick says Australia \"have played a significant amount of Test rugby in recent months,\" which makes the Wallabies' visit the sternest test of England's patched-up squad."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Italy without 15 key men through injury, including captain Michele Lamaro",
